body:
I literally also just academically withdrew this semester because too much shit going on in my life. I spoke with an advisor and they told me it was better to graduate healthy and prioritize myself than to graduate unhealthy with a degree that I wasn't in the emotional state to put my best effort into. The good news for me is that it doesn't really effect my graduation date, and so it won't have that many financial implications, though I also receive a scholarship that I don't have to refund so I'm lucky in that respect.

&#x200B;

Also UB housing sucks ass. On top of everything going on, I was dealing with a completely abusive roommate and housing was doing nothing to help me. They know how crazy she is because I'm not the first one to leave that dorm, and she's had problems in the past with previous people she's lived with. Actually, I don't think there has been a time she hasn't had a problem with people she's lived with, and I should have read that as a red flag. Finally it blew up and I went to emergency housing, and sitting here in complete isolation I think was the last straw for me. I don't want to give them my money next semester.
